        "original_id": "f93b6b41-3c2c-5fb9-94b3-ddc5120f8914",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lukas Rossi, Terry Kath, Ben Moody, Miles McPherson, Josh Newell, Peter Cetera\n- Bands and Projects: Rock Star Supernova, Chicago, The Halo Method, We Are the Fallen, Evanescence, Daylight Division, In This Moment\n- Roles: rock musician, guitarist, vocalist, drummer, bassist, songwriter, lead singer\n- Songs and TV: Brand New Love Affair, CBS Television reality series Rock Star\n\nFacts:\n- Terry Alan Kath was born on January 31, 1946, and he became an American musician and songwriter.\n- Terry Kath was an original guitarist, a lead singer, and a founding member of the rock band Chicago.\n- Lukas Rossi was born on December 21, 1976, and he became a Canadian rock musician.\n- Terry Kath died on January 23, 1978.\n- Lukas Rossi won the CBS Television reality series Rock Star, a televised audition contest to become the lead singer of the hard rock supergroup Rock Star Supernova.\n- The Halo Method consisted of guitarist Ben Moody of We Are the Fallen and formerly Evanescence, drummer Miles McPherson, vocalist Lukas Rossi formerly of Rock Star Supernova and Daylight Division, and bassist Josh Newell formerly of In This Moment.\n- In the song Brand New Love Affair, guitarist Terry Kath sings the first half and bassist Peter Cetera sings the second half.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
